title: Rooms from walls
intro: Wall Rooms finds the rooms a tilemap's walls close off, keeps them up to date as walls change, and says which room anything is in.

project: Empty | Wall Rooms

chapter: Walls make rooms | Wall Rooms on a tilemap
create: Tilemap
rename: Floor
set: Transform.Position = -6, 3.5, 0
set: Tilemap.Tiles = ............\n.1111111111.\n.1....1...1.\n.1....2...1.\n.1....1...1.\n.1111111111.\n............
say: Here is a little building: an outer wall, a wall down the middle and a door in it, tile two.
add: WallRooms
set: WallRooms.Show = true
explain: field:WallRooms.Show | Show | Show tints each closed room a color of its own, so you can see where the walls close rooms off.
expectvalue: Floor.WallRooms.Closed = 2
explain: scene | Scene view | Two closed rooms. The ring of floor outside reaches the map's edge, so it is open to the outside and not tinted.
explain: field:WallRooms.SolidTiles | Solid Tiles | Solid tiles are walls, the same ones grid movers walk round.

chapter: Doors count as shut | Wall Tiles
set: Tilemap.BackgroundTiles = 2
expectvalue: Floor.WallRooms.Closed = 1
say: Make the door a background tile, so people can walk through it, and the two rooms become one.
set: WallRooms.WallTiles = 2
expectvalue: Floor.WallRooms.Closed = 2
explain: field:WallRooms.WallTiles | Wall Tiles | Wall Tiles are walls to rooms even where they can be walked through. List the door's tiles and a door counts as shut, so heat stays in its room.
explain: field:WallRooms.WallLayers | Wall Layers | Walls built as entities count too: solid colliders on these collision layers, over a cell's middle.

chapter: Kept up to date | As walls change
create: Text
rename: Room Count
set: Transform.Position = 0, 4.4, 0
set: Text.Track = Floor
set: Text.Output = Closed
set: Text.Value = {0} closed rooms
explain: field:Text.Output | Output | A text shows Closed, how many rooms the walls close off. RoomArea and RoomId read the room a named entity stands in.
play
wait: 1
say: Now knock a hole in the left room's outer wall while the game runs.
select: Floor
set: Tilemap.Tiles = ............\n.1111111111.\n.1....1...1.\n......2...1.\n.1....1...1.\n.1111111111.\n............
wait: 1
expectvalue: Floor.WallRooms.Closed = 1
say: The left room is open to the outside now, and the count says so. Rooms are worked out again only when the walls change, not every frame, and Changed tells scripts when they have.
stop
say: Each room keeps its id as walls go up and come down, and scripts ask which room a cell, a point or an entity is in, and what is in a room.
